# Copy to .env. Nothing here is required — the app runs with none of these set.
#
# ── Which backend? ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo talks to two different backends, so the choice is a *mode* rather
# than a value you edit by hand:
#
#   npm run dev:local    → http://localhost:3000/api/v1   (.env.localapi)
#   npm run dev:cloud    → the shared hosted API           (.env.cloud)
#   npm run dev          → whatever VITE_API_BASE_URL below says
#
# The active backend is logged to the browser console on boot, so a tab can
# always be traced back to the API it is actually talking to.
#
# Base URL for the FLEETIN backend API. Defaults to localhost:3000 when unset.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1

# Dev-only demo login fallback and the "Try a demo account" picker on the
# login page. Requires import.meta.env.DEV as well, so this has no effect in
# a production build regardless of this value — see README.md "Environment".
# Off by default, including in local dev.
#
# NOTE: the picker only pre-fills the form and grants a *local* session. It
# does not authenticate against a real backend, so every API call from that
# session comes back 401. To use a real backend, sign in normally.
# VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_AUTH=true
